   "text": "This is vancomycin with its vancosamine amine converted to a thiourea. The thiourea is linked through a triethylene-glycol-type chain (three ether oxygens) to a 1,2,3-triazole, and the triazole carries a CH2\u2013purine group. The purine is a 6-amino-2-butoxy-8-hydroxy-purine joined through N9, which makes this a TLR7-agonist conjugate.\n\nI wrote the vancomycin core from memory of its stereo-defined SMILES rather than re-deriving each stereocentre from the wedges. I did not re-check the stereo tags against the drawing, so they are the least certain part of the answer. The thiourea, chain, triazole and purine are plain connectivity with no stereo.\n\nSMILES: C[C@H]1[C@H]([C@@](C[C@@H](O1)O[C@H]2[C@H]([C@@H]([C@H](O[C@H]2OC3=C4C=C5C=C3OC6=C(C=C(C=C6)[C@H]([C@H](C(=O)N[C@H](C(=O)N[C@H]5C(=O)N[C@@H]7C8=CC(=C(C=C8)O)C9=C(C=C(C=C9O)O)[C@H](NC(=O)[C@H]([C@@H](C1=CC(=C(O4)C=C1)Cl)O)NC7=O)C(=O)O)CC(=O)N)NC(=O)[C@@H](CC(C)C)NC)O)Cl)CO)O)O)(C)NC(=S)NCCOCCOCCOCCn%10cc(Cn%11c(O)nc%12c(N)nc(OCCCC)nc%12%11)nn%10)O"
